 not a fixed number of years or a fixed survey method; it’s a context-dependent assessment of whether the combination of survey effort, detectability, and habitat fate leaves any reasonable room for a surviving individual. For insects, that combination is almost always far weaker, which is why scientists are more cautious and why you see those “possibly extinct” or “rediscovered” stories. It’s the same logic working perfectly—it just frequently outputs “we’re not sure yet” instead of “yes, it’s extinct.”
